=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_3a7f — The Nightstand Charger and the Hook Laptop (fork of p_8c4e)

The parent p_8c4e claimed the charger rests at desk_b1 overnight on weekdays with "usually" confidence, but that claim has now gone against 8 consecutive times since the last call. The clock-hour data makes the real pattern clear: from 00:00 to 06:00 every weekday the charger is desk_b1 ×3 and nightstand_b1 ×2 — a 60/40 split, not "usually at the desk." More recently it has been landing on the nightstand. I move the overnight weekday block to nightstand_b1 with "sometimes" confidence, acknowledging the split.

Second, the parent said laptop_hana and pen_hana rest at desk_b1 on "both" days 0–24. But on every single weekend pass (all 12 hours, both Saturday and Sunday) the laptop and pen are at entry_hook_e1 — never at desk_b1. The desk_b1 sightings appear only on weekday nights, and even then it is a 2-2-1 three-way split with entry_hook_e1 and entry_table_e1. I add a weekend override to entry_hook_e1 for both objects.

What sets this apart from p_8c4e: at 02:00 on a weekday, charger_hana is at nightstand_b1 (not desk_b1); at 12:00 on a Saturday, laptop_hana and pen_hana are at entry_hook_e1 (not desk_b1). What would refute it: charger_hana at desk_b1 at 02:00 on a weekday three or more times in a row, or laptop_hana at desk_b1 on any weekend pass.

